WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.620 --> 00:00:07.959
When in the Course of human events, it becomes
necessary for one people to dissolve the political

00:00:07.959 --> 00:00:12.580
bands which have connected them with another,
and to assume among the powers of the earth,

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:15.339
the
separate and equal station to which the Laws

00:00:15.339 --> 00:00:18.810
of Nature and of Nature's God entitle them,
a decent

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:22.689
respect to the opinions of mankind requires
that they should declare the causes which

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:25.050
impel them to
the separation.

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:30.059
We hold these truths to be self-evident, that
all men are created equal, that they are endowed

00:00:30.059 --> 00:00:32.640
by their
Creator with certain unalienable Rights, that

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:36.149
among these are Life, Liberty and the pursuit
of Happiness--

00:00:36.149 --> 00:00:42.260
That to secure these rights, Governments
are instituted among Men, deriving their just

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:47.429
powers from the consent of the governed, --That
whenever any Form of Government becomes

00:00:47.429 --> 00:00:52.190
destructive of these ends, it is the Right
of the People to alter or to abolish it, and

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:56.670
to institute new
Government, laying its foundation on such

00:00:56.670 --> 00:00:59.969
principles and organizing its powers in such
form, as to

00:00:59.969 --> 00:01:05.100
them shall seem most likely to effect their
Safety and Happiness. Prudence, indeed, will

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.760
dictate that
Governments long established should not be

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:11.200
changed for light and transient causes; and
accordingly

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:16.860
all experience hath shewn, that mankind are
more disposed to suffer, while evils are sufferable,

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:20.360
than
to right themselves by abolishing the forms

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:23.630
to which they are accustomed. But when a long
train of

00:01:23.630 --> 00:01:30.680
abuses and usurpations, pursuing invariably
the same Object evinces a design to reduce

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:34.810
them under
absolute Despotism, it is their right, it

00:01:34.810 --> 00:01:39.350
is their duty, to throw off such Government,
and to provide

00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:42.000
new Guards for their future security.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:46.920
We, therefore, the Representatives of the
united States of America, in General Congress,

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:49.250
Assembled,
appealing to the Supreme Judge of the world

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:50.640
for the rectitude of our intentions, do, in
the Name, and

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:59.420
by Authority of the good People of these Colonies,
solemnly publish and declare, That these United

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:05.230
Colonies are, and of Right ought to be Free
and Independent States; that they are Absolved

00:02:05.230 --> 00:02:07.680
from all
Allegiance to the British Crown, and that

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:10.719
all political connection between them and
the State of Great

00:02:10.719 --> 00:02:19.260
Britain, is and ought to be totally dissolved;
and that as Free and Independent States, they

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:22.749
have full
Power to levy War, conclude Peace, contract

00:02:22.749 --> 00:02:25.480
Alliances, establish Commerce, and to do all
other Acts

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:29.819
and Things which Independent States may of
right do. And for the support of this Declaration,

00:02:29.819 --> 00:02:33.549
with a
firm reliance on the protection of divine

00:02:33.549 --> 00:02:37.480
Providence, we mutually pledge to each other
our Lives, our

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:39.449
Fortunes and our sacred Honor.

